Laura (Docs): quick heads-up — I'm drafting a short FAQ + SDK snippet for the new tiered usage credits change. goal: small copy + 1 code snippet per SDK + a grafana panel query example. filing PR later today.

Olivia (DevEx): awesome. can you include an example for per-route meter headers? devs keep asking how to read X-Quota-Remaining vs X-Quota-Window.

Laura (Docs): yes, adding a tiny table and a JS snippet that shows header parsing. also adding a note about burst credits and how they appear in the dashboard.

Kevin (Eng): heads-up — the header names changed in the backend last week. use X-Redwood-Quota-Remaining and X-Redwood-Quota-Window in docs, but mention backwards compat with old X-Quota-* headers. i can add a short middleware example to repo if you want.

Laura (Docs): perfect. could you paste a minimal express middleware here? i'll inline it in the snippet section.

Kevin (Eng): sure:```js
// express middleware to surface quota headers on req.rateInfo
app.use((req, res, next) => {
  const rem = res.getHeader('X-Redwood-Quota-Remaining') || res.getHeader('X-Quota-Remaining');
  const win = res.getHeader('X-Redwood-Quota-Window') || res.getHeader('X-Quota-Window');
  req.rateInfo = { remaining: Number(rem || 0), windowSec: Number(win || 0) };
  next();
});
```

Sasha (PM): note for the FAQ — include an example of what happens on tier downgrade mid-month (proration + grace window). folks ask this a lot.

Laura (Docs): adding a short Q/A: "If you downgrade a tier mid-cycle, credits are prorated and a 7-day grace window applies. Dashboard shows 'pending adjustment' on billing page." short and link to the billing playbook.

Michael (Billing): please don't promise exact days in docs unless we link to billing playbook — the grace window can vary for enterprise. suggest phrasing: "typically a 7-day grace window; see billing playbook for enterprise terms."

Laura (Docs): good call, adjusted wording. thanks.

Olivia (DevEx): for SDK examples, propose these three micro-examples: 1) Node fetch wrapper showing header parse, 2) Python requests example for embedding usage, 3) curl snippet for quick testing. keep each under 6 lines.

Laura (Docs): draft JS SDK example:```js
// node fetch wrapper to surface quota info
const r = await fetch(url, { headers });
const remaining = Number(r.headers.get('X-Redwood-Quota-Remaining') || r.headers.get('X-Quota-Remaining'));
const reset = Number(r.headers.get('X-Redwood-Quota-Window') || 0);
console.log(`tokens left: ${remaining}, window: ${reset}s`);
```

Olivia (DevEx): looks good. can you also add a short tip about using the console's per-route breakdown (link to console panel)? it's a frequent question.

Laura (Docs): will add a one-liner with the console link (docs -> usage analytics -> per-route).

DocsBot: Reminder: docs PR template requires a changelog entry + crosslink to billing playbook if billing impact.

Laura (Docs): thanks DocsBot. adding changelog and a small migration note for SDKs.

Sasha (PM): final ask — include a Grafana panel PromQL example that shows consumed tokens by tier for the last 7d. engineering suggested the following:```promql
sum by(tier) (increase(redwood_tokens_consumed_total{env="prod"}[7d]))
```

Kevin (Eng): that PromQL is ok, but prefer filtering by "customer_tier" label instead of generic "tier". use customer_tier in metrics. also include a note to set the legend to {{customer_tier}}.

Laura (Docs): adjusted grafana snippet:```promql
sum by(customer_tier) (increase(redwood_tokens_consumed_total{env="prod"}[7d]))
```
Legend: {{customer_tier}}

Michael (Billing): can we add a small example of using the dashboard to reconcile credits vs billed tokens? just a note: "use billing exports + the tokens_consumed_total metric for reconciliation" — no deep dive.

Laura (Docs): added one-line reconciliation note and link to the billing export guide.

Olivia (DevEx): quick QA: can someone run the snippets in a smoke check? i'll pull into the quickstart repo and run them.

Kevin (Eng): i'll run the middleware and promql against staging metrics this afternoon.

Laura (Docs): thanks everyone — i'll open the PR at 1758160000 and tag reviewers: @Olivia (DevEx), @Kevin (Eng), @Michael (Billing). aim to merge by EOD. :+1:

Sasha (PM): thanks Laura. small doc wins like this reduce support tickets. :rocket:
